HST Office: Writer style gallery on the Tabbed ribbon shows whole rows only.

Upstream the gallery was a 65 px high scrolled icon view with 36 px rows: a second row cut
off at the bottom and a vertical scrollbar. Now it shows exactly one row of taller previews
(100x52, row 58 px, frame 60 px = the ribbon slot), no scrollbar and no wheel-scroll to a
half row: the view holds one "page" (as many previews as fit the width) and buttons on the
right page through the styles (previous / next) or open all styles in the Styles deck of
the sidebar. Only Writer's Tabbed notebookbar uses this control (Calc has none).

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/runtime/check-style-gallery.py (screenshot analysis) under Xvfb.
